    "updated_at": "2018-06-22T19:09:33Z",
    "body": "One more observation: the two most popular client-side JS cookie libraries https://github.com/js-cookie/js-cookie and https://github.com/ScottHamper/Cookies both accept `expires` options, but if you pass them as numbers, they're interpreted relative to now; you can pass JS `Date` objects if you want to use an absolute timestamp.\r\n\r\nIMO, this is evidence that now-relative expiration (i.e. `max-age`) is the most popular, user-friendly option.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
