    "updated_at": "2018-06-23T09:40:23Z",
    "body": "Thank you for the feedback!\r\n\r\nas-is, `expires` is consistent with `lastModified` in the filesystem API and with the storage model in the cookies RFC. When returning a cookie (in a `CookieListItem`), `expires` needs to be an absolute timestamp, because there's no natural reference point. As a principle, we want writing and reading to use the same format.\r\n\r\nSeparately, I think that `expires: Date.now() + 1000` is more readable than `expires: 1000` -- the unit and reference point is clearer in the former case, rather than the latter case.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
