    "updated_at": "2018-06-25T22:51:30Z",
    "body": "One more thought here: I think a lot of developers will incorrectly write `expires: 1000` in this API; that bug will result in _data loss_ as the cookie expires immediately.\r\n\r\nIf y'all want to stick with `expires`, then I think the API should warn (or maybe even fail) if the user provides an `expires` date that's greater than 0 but less than a very large number, like  `1514764800000` (1/1/2018 UTC) or something.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
