    "body": "> existing APIs makes sense for consistency with HTTP Cookie RFC\r\n\r\n- MaxAge: relative number sec\r\n- Expires: absolute DateTime string\r\n\r\nand Max-Age is better than Expire.\r\n\r\n> If a cookie has both the Max-Age and the Expires attribute, the Max-Age attribute has precedence and controls the expiration date of the cookie. \r\n> --- https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-httpbis-rfc6265bis/#section-4.1.2.2\r\n\r\nsince parsing Expire date time string cause some problem. and max-age was introduced for replacing expires historically.\r\nbut now Cookie Stores expire is not align with both of them.\r\n\r\nIt's consists with other storage api, but not consists with Cookie spec and means not align with current cookie handling manner.\r\n\r\nI'm agree with adding max-age with relative number. or adding clear explanation for design decision.\r\n\r\n",
